# The nttd networks this server serves.
#
# Its own manifest, in its own directory, rather than entries added to the studio's
# registries/manifest.hocon. That file belongs to upstream neuro-san-studio, and editing it means a
# merge conflict on every pull; pointing AGENT_MANIFEST_FILE here instead costs one line of .env.
#
#   AGENT_MANIFEST_FILE=registries/manifest.hocon
#
# FOUR NETWORKS, in two layers.
#
# The PLAYERS take game actions. Both are generated from the nttd-workbench registries and
# reference its coded tools in place, so no game-layer Python is duplicated here — see the header
# of either file for why they are generated rather than included. Both play STEPPED scenarios only:
# the world is paused between steps and the agent advances it explicitly, so deliberation costs no
# game time.
#
# The KNOWLEDGE networks take no game action and hold no session credentials. They read telemetry
# and files, which is what makes it impossible for one of them to spend a game day while thinking
# about one.
#
#   nttd_air_player   plays a session as an air transport company
#   nttd_rail_player  plays it as a rail freight company
#   nttd_planner      runs a session boundary: opens with a plan and claims, closes with verdicts
#   nttd_watcher      wakes mid-session and returns on_track / underperforming / doomed
{
    "nttd_air_player.hocon": true
    "nttd_rail_player.hocon": true
    "nttd_planner.hocon": true
    "nttd_watcher.hocon": true
}
